# Production safety

Production database privileges, server configuration, environment configuration, Nginx configuration, and process configuration all count as production changes.

Do not modify them unless the currently authorised phase explicitly requires and permits that exact change.

## Do not change unless the phase explicitly permits it

- Production PostgreSQL privileges, roles, and grants (including `PUBLIC`)
- Production `.env` / secrets / process environment
- Production Nginx site files and certificates (`api.advisortrack.co.za`, `portal.advisortrack.co.za`)
- Production PM2 process configuration (`advisortrack-api`)
- Production deployment directories and runtime

## Accepted Phase 10 exception

The Phase 10 `PUBLIC CONNECT` revoke on `advisor_track` is accepted and must not be reverted merely for symmetry. Production remained healthy and its application role retains explicit `CONNECT` permission.

## Demo isolation

Demo work must use the separate demo runtime, env, database, Nginx site, and PM2 process. Sharing the physical server/IP is acceptable. Sharing production application state is not.
